{"type":"assistant","uuid":"3532620d-b582-4c0d-811b-93b1a48d0d00","session_id":"d35a6fa7-59d4-4e2a-b6ff-866a09e754cb","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"3532620d-b582-4c0d-811b-93b1a48d0d00","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze this bug report. The issue is about URL/URI parsing where query parameters containing `%26` (`&`) and `%3D` (`=`) are being incorrectly split. \n\nThe URL `https://example.com/?q=a%26b%3Dc` should parse as:\n- `q` → `a&b=c`\n\nBut it's currently parsing as:\n- `q` → `a`\n- `b` → `c`\n\nThis suggests that the code is decoding the URL components and then re-splitting on `&` and `=`, which incorrectly interprets the decoded `&` and `=` as delimiters instead of data.\n\nLet me start by exploring the project structure to understand what we're working with.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
